      "text": "Starting from the given equation, we square both sides to get:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 &= 4^2 \\\\\nx^2 - 2 \\cdot x \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{x^2} &= 16 \\\\\nx^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} - 2 &= 16 \\\\\nx^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} &= 18\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we will find $x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3}$. To do this, we multiply both sides of the equation $x - \\frac{1}{x} = 4$ by $x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}$:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\right) &= 4(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}) \\\\\nx^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} &= 4 \\cdot 18 - 2 \\\\\nx^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} &= 72 - 2 \\\\\n\\boxed{70}\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{70}$.",
